# Allowlist for .github/claims/metadata-claims.py (run it for the rules).
#
# Every line that says "metadata-only" (or "metadata only", "somente
# metadados", "solo metadatos") must be here. A line qualifies when it names
# which connector it means: the hosted metadata connector (api.…/mcp, the
# pilot's server.mjs, self-hosted containers, 'metadata' connections, the
# 'provided' credential source), or 2a's attested reader as it was before 2b;
# or when it is about something else entirely. A general claim that "the
# hosted connector" cannot read content is not allowed: since 2b the attested
# reader at mcp.…/mcp can, for 'content' connections.
#
#   <path>                 every hit in the file (code; give the reason)
#   <path> :: <fragment>   only hits whose line contains the fragment

# Unrelated meanings of the phrase.
deploy/enclave/Dockerfile :: # metadata-only directory changes: /app and the apk directories
docs/media-security.md :: Begin with metadata-only counts and ambiguous object
docs/rest-api.md :: The server filters routing metadata only, never plaintext.
internal/store/scan.go :: ScanFilter describes routing metadata only.
internal/wsapi/readmodel.go :: DeviceFromRow contains stored metadata only.

# History: the 2026-09-21 decision, now marked superseded for the attested reader.
docs/decisions.md :: ## Hosted remote MCP is metadata-only (2026-09-21)

# This gate's own CI job explains the rule.
.github/workflows/ci.yml :: sentence calling "the hosted connector" metadata-only is false unless it

# The lead's contract: 2a as it shipped, the pilot's reader, and this gate's own pattern.
docs/mcp-enclave.md :: 2a is **metadata-only**: no message text
docs/mcp-enclave.md :: The pilot's reader (`server.mjs` as `wappie-mcp`) stays metadata-only
docs/mcp-enclave.md :: the CI grep gate (`metadata-only

